            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0477" n="465" xml:id="pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.199/66: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-08T19:00:00+00:00">December 8, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 8—3:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>409. Bay’s telegram of December 6, 11 a.m. Military Commandant at Irun received
                    Queipo de Llano’s telegram urging him to facilitate Chapman’s return to Bilbao
                    but regrets that Sangroniz’s orders make it impossible to grant the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">salvo conducto</hi>. He is calling the General’s
                    telegram to the attention of the diplomatic cabinet. Under the circumstances
                    Chapman leaves on the 15th and I shall do no more in the Bilbao matter for the
                    present.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
